  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Pain & Cie is at the entrance to the flower market, at 3 rue Louis Gassin on Cours Saleya. According to its website, the same family has run it for three generations, at this spot for 26 years, about 30 metres from the Promenade des Anglais and a few seconds on foot from the beach. The dining room mixes light wood and cream tones, and the sunny terrace looks onto the market bustle.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The restaurant's website does not mention animals. Its booking page (pain-cie.eatbu.com) lists "pets allowed" among its services, and the Qualidog entry in the emmenetonchien.com directory, which is not an official source, reports a welcome for dogs with a water bowl on arrival and no dog supplement. None of these pages says whether a dog may come inside or must stay on the terrace.</p>
      <p>Service is continuous, every day from 8am to 10:30pm. Breakfast is served until noon according to the website, which also mentions weekend brunch, a coffee shop and evening opening in summer. The menu has two daily specials under €20, renewed each day from the morning's deliveries, mixed salads, bowls, a vegetarian burger with homemade ratatouille and protein formulas. The whole menu is available to take away, for a meal facing the sea. Booking is not compulsory, but the website recommends it at weekends and on public holidays, especially for the terrace. The phone number is 04 93 62 94 32.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: one phone call is enough to confirm the dog welcome and ask whether a terrace table is possible.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant's website places it about 30 metres from the Promenade des Anglais and a few seconds on foot from the beach, with takeaway dishes for a picnic facing the Baie des Anges.</p>
    </div>

